__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.idea/

# ForgePilot runtime state (sessions, worktrees, repo mirrors, logs)
.forgepilot/

# Local environment overrides — may hold credentials. Never commit this.
.env.local
.env

# Workspace-private documents: instructions and design records written for whoever is
# working in *this* directory, not for whoever clones it. `CLAUDE.md` is the file a harness
# injects into the model's context, and `ForgePilot文档.md` / `docs/实现方案.md` are the two
# documents it names as the sources of intent and of the build decisions. Each belongs to a
# workspace, so each is kept here and never committed — they were tracked once and were
# removed from the history too, and a clone gets the code, `docs/notes/` and `README.md`.
# `tests/contract/test_the_workspace_instructions_fit_the_budget.py` is the guard on the
# front door and skips when the file is not in the checkout.
CLAUDE.md
ForgePilot文档.md
docs/实现方案.md

# `pytest --cov` writes this beside whatever directory it ran in, so the gate left an
# untracked file in the repository root the first time it was run. Output, not source.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Generated knowledge-graph output (the /graphify skill). Build artefact: large,
# derived, and regenerated on demand — it has no business in the history.
graphify-out/

# Eval results and scratch repos. Output, not source: a run is reproduced by
# running it, and a committed result file is a claim nobody can check.
evals/results/
# Vestigial: scratch moved to `$FORGEPILOT_HOME/eval-scratch` because keeping it
# inside the repo put the eval's own answers one `..` from the agent's workspace,
# and created a nested git repository per worktree. Kept so an old checkout that
# still writes here cannot commit it.
evals/scratch/

# A writable temp root *inside* the workspace. Needed on a host whose spawned
# process tree cannot write to `%TEMP%` — this development box confines a command
# to the session workspace, so `tempfile.gettempdir()` falls back to the current
# directory and every `pytest` run drops its `tmp_path` tree (thousands of files)
# into the repository root. ForgePilot's own `mkdtemp(prefix="forgepilot-s-")`
# workspaces land in the same place.
#
# Nothing has to be exported any more: `tests/conftest.py` pins the temp root here when
# it would otherwise be the repository, and `LocalTempWorkspacePlugin` refuses the
# fallback outright unless its row names a `base_dir` or `FORGEPILOT_TMP` does.
.tmp/
# The belt for that first case, kept for a run that does not load that conftest:
# ignored so one forgotten variable cannot commit a few thousand generated files.
pytest-of-*/
